  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3cc01392",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Most importantly, the coordinates of the selected binding site are also assigned to the `Protein` object in the project:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "b3cc21d0",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Protein.binding_site_coordinates\n",
    "# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9cf7ec2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id='Ligand-similarity-search'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### II.4 [Ligand similarity search](#Contents-in-Practical)\n",
    "\n",
    "With the coordinates of the protein's **binding site** in hand, we now focus on the **ligand similarity search** stage of the pipeline. This step is implemented in the **`LigandSimilaritySearch`** class, which takes **`Ligand`** and **`Specs.LigandSimilaritySearch`** objects as input and initializes a **similarity search** using the **PubChem** web server with the help of functions implemented in the **`pubchem`** helper module.\n",
    "\n",
    "Several **drug-likeness scores** are then automatically calculated for each of the retrieved **analogs** using the **`rdkit`** module. Based on these scores, a user-specified number (defined in the **input file**) of the **most drug-like analogs** are selected. These analogs are then used to create new **`Ligand`** objects with the **`Ligand`** class introduced earlier. Finally, these objects are assigned as **instance attributes** of both the **`LigandSimilaritySearch`** object and the original **`Ligand`** object."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5082dc12",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<details>\n",
    "\n",
    "<summary> Click here for additional information about the drug-likeness scores </summary> \n",
    "\n",
    "`drug_score_total` is calculated as a weighted average of the following three drug-likeness scores, with a ratio of 3:2:1, respectively:\n",
    "\n",
    "* `drug_score_qed`: Quantitative Estimate of Drug-likeness (QED) [calculated by *RDKit*](https://www.rdkit.org/docs/source/rdkit.Chem.QED.html) using default parameters.\n",
    "* `drug_score_custom`: QED calculated by implementing functions that fit experimental data from [G. Bickerton *et al.*, *Nat. Chem* **2012**, 4(2), 90-98.](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3524573/)\n",
    "* `drug_score_lipinski`: [Lipinski's rule of 5](https://doi.org/10.1016/S0169-409X(96)00423-1) (normalized, i.e. 4 = 1, 3 = 0.75, 2 = 0.5, 1 = 0.25, 0 = 0)\n",
    "    \n",
    "</details>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "18975772",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We instantiate the class and assign it to our project:\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note*: For this project, this process will take **about 2 minutes** to complete.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note*: This is the first place in the pipeline where we are using frozen data (see [here](#frozen_data))."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "965a9682",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from utils import LigandSimilaritySearch\n",
    "\n",
    "project1.LigandSimilaritySearch = LigandSimilaritySearch(\n",
    "    ligand_obj=project1.Ligand,\n",
    "    similarity_search_specs_obj=project1.Specs.LigandSimilaritySearch,\n",
    "    similarity_search_output_path=project1.Specs.OutputPaths.similarity_search,\n",
    "    frozen_data_filepath=frozen_data_project1.pubchem_similarity_search,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "fca99158",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "(30, 14)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 27,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
