  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d7bebc6",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "<a id='Docking-calculations'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### II.5 [Docking calculations](#Contents-in-Practical)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "We have now successfully:\n",
    "\n",
    "* defined the **binding site** of the input **protein**\n",
    "* identified a set of the most **drug-like analogs** for the input **ligand**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eb16c317",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The next step in the pipeline is to perform **docking calculations** on the **protein binding site** using the **ligand analogs**. This is done automatically by the **`Docking`** class of the pipeline, which:\n",
    "\n",
    "* prepares the **structures for docking** using the **Pybel module** of the **OpenBabel package** (implemented in the **`obabel` helper module**),\n",
    "* docks all provided **analogs** onto the protein using the **Smina program** (implemented in the **`smina` helper module**),\n",
    "* and processes the **docking results** and stores them separately for each **docking pose**. \n",
    "\n",
    "Other meaningful **information** is also extracted from the results of all **docking poses** for each **analog** and stored separately as new **attributes** for that analog's **`Ligand` object**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d3bf40d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We instantiate the **`Docking`** class with:\n",
    "\n",
    "* the **`Protein`** object containing the **binding site coordinates**\n",
    "* the list of **analogs** (as **`Ligand`** objects)\n",
    "* and the **`Specs.Docking`** object of the project"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d4d1b9a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "*Note*: This is the most computationally intense process of the pipeline and will take **5 to 10 minutes** (for 20 ligands) to complete.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note*: This is the second place in the pipeline where we are using frozen data (see [here](#frozen_data))."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "95051f4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can now view all the calculated docking results for each docking pose of each analog: "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "1025b18d-3b98-47d2-a38e-393f660f3cba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(hasattr(project1, \"Docking\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "28a61255",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "AttributeError",
     "evalue": "'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'Docking'",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m                            Traceback (most recent call last)",
      "Cell \u001b[0;32mIn[45], line 1\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m----> 1\u001b[0m \u001b[43mproject1\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241;43m.\u001b[39;49m\u001b[43mDocking\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241m.\u001b[39mresults_dataframe\u001b[38;5;241m.\u001b[39mshape\n\u001b[1;32m      2\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;66;03m# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT\u001b[39;00m\n",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m: 'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'Docking'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "project1.Docking.results_dataframe.shape\n",
    "# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9a831b32",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Docking.results_dataframe.sort_values(by=\"affinity[kcal/mol]\").head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00501c41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "From the docking output we obtain ```affinity```, which is the estimated binding affinity from the docking score, along with pose distances from the best predicted binding mode, calculated using different methods (```best mode_rmsd_l.b``` and ```best mode_rmsd_u.b```)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8d175af",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<details>\n",
    "\n",
    "<summary> Click here for additional information about the Smina output.</summary> \n",
    "\n",
    "From the [*Autodock Vina* manual](http://vina.scripps.edu/manual/):\n",
    "\n",
    "RMSD values are calculated relative to the best mode and use only movable heavy atoms. Two variants of RMSD metrics are provided, rmsd/lb (RMSD lower bound) and rmsd/ub (RMSD upper bound), differing in how the atoms are matched in the distance calculation:\n",
    "\n",
    "* $rmsd/ub$ (upper bound) matches each atom in one conformation with itself in the other conformation, ignoring any symmetry\n",
    "* $rmsd/lb$ (lower bound) is defined as follows: $rmsd/lb(c1, c2) = max(rmsd'(c1, c2), rmsd'(c2, c1))$, i.e. a match between each atom in one conformation with the *closest* atom of the same element type in the other conformation.\n",
    "    \n",
    "</details>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ac17816d",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_affinity_pose = project1.Docking.results_dataframe.sort_values(by=\"affinity[kcal/mol]\").index[\n",
    "    0\n",
    "]\n",
    "value = project1.Docking.results_dataframe.loc[best_affinity_pose][\"affinity[kcal/mol]\"]\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    f\"Predicted best ranking molecule (CID): {best_affinity_pose[0]}, predicted affinity value below -10.0 [kcal/mol]:{value<-10.}.\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6373a3e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Alternatively, by accessing a specific analog, we can view the full results for that analog using the attribute `dataframe_docking`:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2014dd58",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"].dataframe_docking"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7433c411",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A summary of the docking results (e.g. highest/mean binding affinities) are also added to the main dataframe of each analog and can be viewed by calling its object. Here showing only the relevant data, i.e. the last 7 rows:     "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "53fbe8ec",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"]().tail(7)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "92d6c9df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The same summary data are also added as instance attributes for each object, e.g.:\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5797b940",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"].binding_affinity_best"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76902ac6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### II.5.1 Visualizing the docking poses"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4198b93",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The **`py3Dmol` helper module** provides additional **visualization methods** to the **`Docking`** class for displaying the **docking poses**. For example, we can view **all poses** together in an **interactive** manner using the **`visualize_all_poses`** method. In this method, poses are **sorted by their binding affinities** and labeled by their **CID** and corresponding **pose number**. By selecting an **analog** from the menu below, the viewer automatically displays the **protein residues** within **6 Å** of the **ligand**, along with its corresponding **binding affinity**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9237f679",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Also if we are interested in visualization of a certain analog's docking poses, we can use the `visualize_analog_poses` method instead, and provide the analog's CID."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f4ded9d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Note: Clicking through different ligands and docking poses works only when you execute this talktorial; it does not work on the website version of the talktorial.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "2e3bc5e0-9de1-45cb-9bf9-f22d2f279b92",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "AttributeError",
     "evalue": "'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'Docking'",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m                            Traceback (most recent call last)",
      "Cell \u001b[0;32mIn[36], line 1\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m----> 1\u001b[0m \u001b[43mproject1\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241;43m.\u001b[39;49m\u001b[43mDocking\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241m.\u001b[39mvisualize_all_poses()\n",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m: 'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'Docking'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "project1.Docking.visualize_all_poses()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea464061",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now let's separately dock the input ligand in order to be able to compare the results later and see how the analogs compare to the starting ligand.\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f6faee17",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.Docking = Docking(\n",
    "    protein_obj=project1.Protein,\n",
    "    list_ligand_obj=[project1.Ligand],\n",
    "    docking_specs_obj=project1.Specs.Docking,\n",
    "    docking_output_path=project1.Specs.OutputPaths.ligand,\n",
    "    frozen_data_filepath=frozen_data_project1.docking_pdbqt_files,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b33273e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Similar to the analogs, the docking results of the input ligand is also stored in its object. \n",
    "\n",
    "For example, to see the docking dataframe:\n",
    "   "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "14adc775",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.dataframe_docking"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4770df8b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "value = project1.Ligand.dataframe_docking.loc[1][\"affinity[kcal/mol]\"]\n",
    "print(f\"Predicted affinity value for pose 1 of input ligand <= -8.5 [kcal/mol]: {value <= -8.5}.\")\n",
    "# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c09e0ad9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Comparing these results, we can already see that the pipeline has identified an **analog** with an estimated **binding affinity** that is **16% higher** than that of the **input ligand** (**-10.2 kcal/mol** versus **-8.8 kcal/mol**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8bb3717",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id='Analysis-of-protein&mdash;ligand-interactions'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### II.6 [Analysis of protein&mdash;ligand interactions](#Contents-in-Practical)\n",
    "With the **docking poses** of each **analog** in hand, we can now focus on analyzing the **protein–ligand interactions** in each **docking pose** of each **analog**. For this analysis, we use the functionalities of the **PLIP package** (*Protein–Ligand Interaction Profiler*), for which we have implemented the **`plip` helper module**. This is then used in the **`InteractionAnalysis` class** of the pipeline, which automatically calculates all **interaction information** for each **docked pose** of each **ligand**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3591a0aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The **`InteractionAnalysis`** class can be instantiated by providing:\n",
    "\n",
    "* the **PDBQT** and **PDB file paths** of the separated **protein structure**\n",
    "* the **first residue number** in the protein\n",
    "* a list of all **analogs** (as **`Ligand` objects**)\n",
    "* the **results DataFrame** of the **docking process**\n",
    "* the **`Specs.InteractionAnalysis`** object of the project\n",
    "* and the **output path** for storing the **interaction analysis data**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "842a43d1-85e1-4256-a905-438a35e5ff17",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('g')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3e8e3cfc-cdaf-4c24-a4c6-3c2736939422",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=DeprecationWarning, module=\"plip\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e93a5480",
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true,
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from utils import InteractionAnalysis\n",
    "\n",
    "project1.InteractionAnalysis = InteractionAnalysis(\n",
    "    separated_protein_pdbqt_filepath=project1.Docking.pdbqt_filepath_extracted_protein,\n",
    "    separated_protein_pdb_filepath=project1.Docking.pdb_filepath_extracted_protein,\n",
    "    protein_first_residue_number=project1.Protein.residue_number_first,\n",
    "    list_ligand_obj=list(project1.Ligand.analogs.values()),\n",
    "    docking_master_df=project1.Docking.master_df,\n",
    "    interaction_analysis_specs_obj=project1.Specs.InteractionAnalysis,\n",
    "    interaction_analysis_output_path=project1.Specs.OutputPaths.interaction_analysis,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3303ba4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The interactions can now be inspected collectively for all docking poses of all analogs. Here, only the number of interactions are recorded for each interaction type:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f49f84d1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.InteractionAnalysis.results.sort_values(\n",
    "    by=\"total_num_interactions\", ascending=False\n",
    ").head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2142af0c",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "min_affinity = -10.0\n",
    "min_total_num_interactions = 11\n",
    "\n",
    "best_interaction_and_score_df = project1.InteractionAnalysis.results[\n",
    "    project1.InteractionAnalysis.results[\"affinity[kcal/mol]\"] < min_affinity\n",
    "]\n",
    "best_interaction_and_score_df = best_interaction_and_score_df[\n",
    "    best_interaction_and_score_df[\"total_num_interactions\"] >= min_total_num_interactions\n",
    "]\n",
    "best_pose = best_interaction_and_score_df.index[0]\n",
    "value = best_interaction_and_score_df.loc[best_pose][\"total_num_interactions\"]\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    f\"Molecule CID: {best_pose[0]} has \"\n",
    "    f\"highest number of interactions >= {min_total_num_interactions}: \"\n",
    "    f\"{value >= min_total_num_interactions}.\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "# NBVAL_CHECK_OUTPUT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c9204095",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If we are interested in the details of a specific **interaction type** for a specific **docking pose**, we can access this information from the corresponding **`Ligand` object** of the **analog**.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, the **hydrophobic interactions** of the **first docking pose** for **analog 65997** can be accessed from its corresponding **`Ligand` object** (showing only the **first five entries**):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b2bb36bb",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"].docking_pose_1_interactions_hydrophobic.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7bfd795",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Or hydrogen-bond interactions of the second docking pose for analog 11292933:    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e30592c1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"].docking_pose_2_interactions_h_bond.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00824e79",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Again, a **summary of the interaction analysis** is added to each **analog's main DataFrame**, which can be viewed by accessing its corresponding **`Ligand` object**. Here, only the **relevant data** (i.e., the **last nine rows**) are shown:    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e4945e7c",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.analogs[\"11292933\"]().tail(9)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "913aca36",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "By using the **`plot_interaction_affinity_correlation`** method, we can also examine whether there is a visible **correlation** between the calculated **binding affinities** and the **number of protein–ligand interactions** for each **docking pose**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c97d7fd5",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "nbsphinx-thumbnail"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.InteractionAnalysis.plot_interaction_affinity_correlation()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c5b65af8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We see that no obvious correlation is visible between the two sets of data; the number of total interactions is weakly correlated with the binding affinity, albeit with several outliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf9d8edd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now let's also analyze the interactions in the docking poses of the input ligand for comparison:    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9fdea9bb",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.InteractionAnalysis = InteractionAnalysis(\n",
    "    project1.Docking.pdbqt_filepath_extracted_protein,\n",
    "    project1.Docking.pdb_filepath_extracted_protein,\n",
    "    project1.Protein.residue_number_first,\n",
    "    [project1.Ligand],\n",
    "    project1.Ligand.Docking.master_df,\n",
    "    project1.Specs.InteractionAnalysis,\n",
    "    project1.Specs.OutputPaths.ligand,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a170c32b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The results can be viewed in a similar way to the analogs. For example, to view the summary data:    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fced88c2",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.Ligand.InteractionAnalysis.results.sort_values(\n",
    "    by=\"total_num_interactions\", ascending=False\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86e86cd6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Again, we see that the pipeline has successfully found analogs that have docking poses with higher number of interactions (up to 12) than those of the input ligand (up to 8)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ee33190",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### II.6.1 Visual interaction analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Thanks to the `py3Dmol` helper module, we have additional methods available in the `InteractionAnalysis` class for visualization of the protein-ligand interactions. For example, we can now view the interactions for all docking poses in an interactive way. By selecting each docking pose from the menu (labeled by their CID and mode-number and sorted by their binding affinities), all the interacting residues are shown. The interactions are visualized with colored lines, for which a color-map is also provided."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d76a53d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Alternatively, if we are interested in visualization of a certain analog's interactions, we can use the `visualize_analog_interactions` method instead, and provide the analog's CID.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0a18221",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "***Note*: Clicking through different ligands and docking poses works only when you execute this talktorial; it does not work on the website version of the talktorial.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cd8316aa",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.InteractionAnalysis.visualize_all_interactions()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb2e8e40",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### II.6.2 Finding poses with specific interactions\n",
    "\n",
    "We can also search for docking poses displaying a specific set of interactions with specific residues of the protein, using the `find_poses_with_specific_interactions` method. This returns a list of tuples, where the first tuple element is the CID, and the second element is its corresponding docking pose number in which the specified interaction exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "We can provide a set of desired interactions to the function, and specify whether we are looking for docking poses that exhibit all or any of these interactions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bd8ba4bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For example, since it's a common interaction in many kinase inhibitors, we can search for the ligands that are involved in hydrogen-bonding with the hinge region of the protein (i.e. residue M793 in EGFR): "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "b25388d6",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "AttributeError",
     "evalue": "'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'InteractionAnalysis'",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m                            Traceback (most recent call last)",
      "Cell \u001b[0;32mIn[35], line 2\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      1\u001b[0m analog_poses_with_desired_interactions \u001b[38;5;241m=\u001b[39m (\n\u001b[0;32m----> 2\u001b[0m     \u001b[43mproject1\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241;43m.\u001b[39;49m\u001b[43mInteractionAnalysis\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;241m.\u001b[39mfind_poses_with_specific_interactions(\n\u001b[1;32m      3\u001b[0m         list_interaction_data\u001b[38;5;241m=\u001b[39m[[\u001b[38;5;124m\"\u001b[39m\u001b[38;5;124mh_bond\u001b[39m\u001b[38;5;124m\"\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;5;241m793\u001b[39m]], all_or_any\u001b[38;5;241m=\u001b[39m\u001b[38;5;124m\"\u001b[39m\u001b[38;5;124many\u001b[39m\u001b[38;5;124m\"\u001b[39m\n\u001b[1;32m      4\u001b[0m     )\n\u001b[1;32m      5\u001b[0m )\n\u001b[1;32m      7\u001b[0m analog_poses_with_desired_interactions\n",
      "\u001b[0;31mAttributeError\u001b[0m: 'LeadOptimizationPipeline' object has no attribute 'InteractionAnalysis'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "analog_poses_with_desired_interactions = (\n",
    "    project1.InteractionAnalysis.find_poses_with_specific_interactions(\n",
    "        list_interaction_data=[[\"h_bond\", 793]], all_or_any=\"any\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "analog_poses_with_desired_interactions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0fe47952",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Using the `visualize_docking_poses_interactions` method, we can also visualize the results separately instead of looking for them in the menu of the viewer above. This method takes a list of docking poses (as tuples, where the first elements are the CIDs, and the second elements are the docking pose numbers; i.e. exactly the output format of `find_poses_with_specific_interactions`) and visualizes them:    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b71ddbd2",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "project1.InteractionAnalysis.visualize_docking_poses_interactions(\n",
    "    list_of_cid_pose_nr_tuples=analog_poses_with_desired_interactions\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1dbb953e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id='Selection-of-the-best-analog'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### **II.7 [Selection of the Best Analog](#Contents-in-Practical)**\n",
    "\n",
    "At this point, we have completed all the **pipeline stages** and gathered all the resulting **data** in our **`LeadOptimizationPipeline`** instance, i.e., **`project1`**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "097dbcff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To recap, we have:\n",
    "\n",
    "* identified the most suitable **binding site** in the input **protein** based on the **project specifications**\n",
    "* gathered a set of **ligand analogs** and filtered them to retain those with the highest **drug-likeness scores**\n",
    "* calculated multiple **docking poses** and corresponding **binding affinities** for each **analog**, and analyzed their **protein–ligand interactions**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f314a173",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we import the **`OptimizedLigands`** class, which takes the **entire project** as input and, based on the **specifications** defined in the **input file**, selects the **best ligand analog(s)**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "bd6013b3-257c-43c1-bd51-3d0f86252a2f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"f\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "19cf517d",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from utils import OptimizedLigands\n",
    "\n",
    "project1.OptimizedLigands = OptimizedLigands(project=project1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3f4ad593-4ee8-4634-8a43-91d63c240847",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  }
